WEBVTT

00:01.530 --> 00:04.670
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.670 --> 00:08.200
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.320 --> 00:27.960
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.960 --> 00:33.860
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.860 --> 00:42.800
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.800 --> 00:47.510
Like the wind

00:47.510 --> 00:50.580
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.580 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.660
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.660 --> 01:07.400
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.400 --> 01:13.540
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.540 --> 01:20.210
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.210 --> 01:27.510
The roadless journey continues

01:49.040 --> 01:52.100
They arrived...

01:53.480 --> 01:55.910
This is the place?

01:55.910 --> 01:57.640
Ellis?

01:59.780 --> 02:01.870
It's warm.

02:04.890 --> 02:08.420
...at this place, where answers await them.

02:08.420 --> 02:10.050
Here we go.

02:33.980 --> 02:38.120
The town was destroyed by
a mysterious epidemic, eh?

02:38.120 --> 02:39.620
It's too perfect.

02:39.620 --> 02:42.590
It just screams "camouflage."

02:42.590 --> 02:44.750
Ellis, which way?

02:47.360 --> 02:49.760
- What?
- Oh, no...

02:49.760 --> 02:51.300
Can you tell what direction or anything?

02:51.300 --> 02:53.300
Sensing anything from the Inca rose?

02:53.300 --> 02:55.640
Straight.

02:55.640 --> 02:58.540
Straight, huh? Roger that.

03:02.480 --> 03:05.540
What is this? This sense of foreboding...

03:07.780 --> 03:09.770
Intruder confirmed.

03:13.560 --> 03:19.130
This really does suit me better.

03:19.130 --> 03:21.190
What about you...

03:23.700 --> 03:25.790
...Miss Hayward?

03:29.370 --> 03:30.970
Do you have a cold?

03:30.970 --> 03:32.340
Oh, no...

03:32.340 --> 03:34.810
It is dry here, so please be careful.

03:34.810 --> 03:37.000
Yes, thank you.

03:38.580 --> 03:43.750
You look more gorgeous without glasses.

03:53.030 --> 03:56.030
It just keeps looking worse and worse.

03:56.030 --> 04:00.590
It's more like they wrecked it,
than that it fell to ruin...

04:02.270 --> 04:03.900
What's wrong?

04:05.440 --> 04:07.070
Ellis?

04:09.110 --> 04:10.910
Ellis!

04:19.020 --> 04:20.950
Do you recognize it?

04:26.860 --> 04:28.450
Ellis?

04:34.770 --> 04:36.570
Ellis?

04:48.220 --> 04:49.780
Ellis!

04:49.780 --> 04:51.820
- That hurts.
- What?

04:51.820 --> 04:53.250
That hurts, Nadie.

04:53.250 --> 04:55.720
Oh, sorry.

04:55.720 --> 04:57.830
What am I doing?

04:57.830 --> 04:59.430
- I know it.
- What?

04:59.430 --> 05:01.260
That.

05:03.160 --> 05:05.430
I want to try going there. It's okay, right?

05:05.430 --> 05:07.240
Yeah...

05:07.240 --> 05:09.070
All right, let's go and see.

05:09.070 --> 05:10.800
Yes.

05:25.450 --> 05:27.350
You can come out now.

05:30.260 --> 05:32.190
That way, huh?

05:39.870 --> 05:41.490
Bulletproof?

05:47.010 --> 05:49.880
So, the biohazard's fake, after all.

05:49.880 --> 05:51.650
Why are they shooting at us?

05:51.650 --> 05:53.950
- Because we're an inconvenience, I'm sure.
- inconvenience?

05:53.950 --> 05:56.020
They want to exterminate the bugs.

05:56.020 --> 05:58.620
Nadie, you're a bug?

05:58.620 --> 06:00.210
Hey, now...

06:08.560 --> 06:11.470
We can do this. Ellis.

06:11.470 --> 06:14.140
When I give the signal, jump inside there.

06:14.140 --> 06:15.540
The window?

06:15.540 --> 06:17.640
I'll be right behind you.

06:17.640 --> 06:19.300
Yessir.

06:29.050 --> 06:30.820
Now, Ellis. Go!

06:30.820 --> 06:32.310
Go!

06:39.560 --> 06:41.500
All right.

06:41.500 --> 06:44.670
- Nadie.
- No! Keep your head down!

06:44.670 --> 06:46.330
Go hide somewhere!

06:46.330 --> 06:48.030
Yessir.

06:53.040 --> 06:56.200
Whoops, I'd forgotten about the driver.

07:03.050 --> 07:04.920
Nadie...

07:20.600 --> 07:23.370
If only there were some
grenades lying around here...

07:23.370 --> 07:24.960
Nadie...

07:36.550 --> 07:38.820
Oh, Ellis...

07:58.840 --> 08:01.780
That's great, Ellis!

08:03.410 --> 08:06.350
All right, it's sink or swim.

08:06.350 --> 08:08.420
No, there's just no way.

08:08.420 --> 08:10.780
Since it's come to this,
maybe I'll try playing dead.

08:25.670 --> 08:27.160
Now's my chance!

08:48.190 --> 08:49.880
Good work.

08:54.900 --> 08:56.520
Ellis?

08:59.500 --> 09:01.330
Ellis...

09:24.360 --> 09:26.490
I know...

09:31.330 --> 09:34.700
Yes, you know.

09:45.950 --> 09:48.050
It's calling.

09:48.050 --> 09:51.350
Yes, it's calling.

09:51.350 --> 09:55.550
It's calling, Ellis.

10:02.530 --> 10:04.760
I told her to stay hidden!

10:27.390 --> 10:30.260
Was the epidemic actually real?

11:06.160 --> 11:07.460
It has been a long time.

11:07.460 --> 11:09.130
What did you want to talk to me about?

11:09.130 --> 11:12.500
Yes, I was hoping to obtain your assistance.

11:27.350 --> 11:29.010
Ellis?

11:46.300 --> 11:49.140
It's hot.

11:49.140 --> 11:50.800
Hold it.

12:25.870 --> 12:28.100
Hey, there, Ellis.

12:29.710 --> 12:31.050
Blood...

12:31.050 --> 12:33.050
Oh, I'm sorry.

12:33.050 --> 12:36.050
I've sullied you, haven't I?

12:36.050 --> 12:38.210
How could I, of all people...

12:43.520 --> 12:48.120
- Nadie...
- She's fine. She's just passed out.

12:50.400 --> 12:53.370
Ellis.

12:53.370 --> 12:55.300
Who are you?

12:55.300 --> 12:58.740
Right now, it still doesn't matter who I am.

12:58.740 --> 13:04.110
But eventually, I'll become
an important part of your life.

13:04.110 --> 13:05.910
No, you won't.

13:10.220 --> 13:12.890
Who are you? A bounty hunter?

13:12.890 --> 13:16.580
I'll be watching you always.

13:18.060 --> 13:22.100
That's what I came to tell you.

13:22.100 --> 13:24.230
You said you'd always be watching...

13:24.230 --> 13:27.740
Yes, I've been watching, Ellis.

13:27.740 --> 13:30.400
- Watching you always.
- Why?

13:30.400 --> 13:35.110
I told you, remember?
That you're important to me.

13:35.110 --> 13:38.410
I told you that you're wrong.

14:10.950 --> 14:14.720
I won't hurt you or anything.

14:14.720 --> 14:18.620
I want to tell you what you want to know.

14:18.620 --> 14:20.150
What I...

14:20.150 --> 14:23.020
That's why you came here, isn't it?

14:25.630 --> 14:28.490
As might be expected,
there's nothing left here...

14:40.040 --> 14:41.640
Did you know that long ago,

14:41.640 --> 14:45.310
there was a group of people
who were called witches?

14:45.310 --> 14:46.480
Witches?

14:46.480 --> 14:52.250
They could manipulate wind...
manipulate flames...

14:52.250 --> 14:56.050
But the witches died out.

15:00.530 --> 15:02.520
What are these?

15:07.000 --> 15:11.030
And so, they created artificial witches.

15:14.170 --> 15:17.510
And that's you, Ellis.

15:34.530 --> 15:37.700
The situation's starting to get nasty...

15:37.700 --> 15:40.200
I was made?

15:40.200 --> 15:44.540
Many life forms were created
with the DNA of witches.

15:44.540 --> 15:49.380
But they all turned out to be failures.

15:49.380 --> 15:51.210
With the exception of you...

15:51.210 --> 15:55.250
...and me.

15:55.250 --> 15:59.420
I'm the same, too, Ellis.

15:59.420 --> 16:03.720
I'm male, so I can't use
the powers that you can...

16:05.230 --> 16:08.900
...but I'm far superior to human beings.

16:08.900 --> 16:12.400
Far, far superior.

16:12.400 --> 16:14.440
What happened to everyone?

16:14.440 --> 16:18.430
Right now, the only ones
who exist in this world...

16:20.340 --> 16:22.470
...are you and me.

16:30.250 --> 16:32.950
Then, what I saw earlier was...

16:52.610 --> 16:57.440
You don't have good command
of your witch's powers yet.

16:57.440 --> 17:00.310
You only exercise it involuntarily.

17:00.310 --> 17:04.790
But in time, you'll be able to
consciously use your powers.

17:04.790 --> 17:06.890
You have no need to worry.

17:06.890 --> 17:10.520
Did I kill the Doctor with those powers?

17:10.520 --> 17:12.290
The Doctor?

17:12.290 --> 17:14.460
Oh, you mean the man who took you in

17:14.460 --> 17:18.500
and was conducting research on you?

17:18.500 --> 17:20.070
Tell me.

17:20.070 --> 17:22.040
I don't know.

17:23.500 --> 17:26.970
But that kind of thing isn't a big issue,

17:26.970 --> 17:28.640
Ellis.

17:39.420 --> 17:44.590
After all, humans are nothing
but foolish, insignificant creatures.

17:46.330 --> 17:49.930
Now, come with me, Ellis.

17:49.930 --> 17:51.920
We'll begin together...

17:56.000 --> 17:58.230
I hate you.

18:01.680 --> 18:03.580
I really hate you.

18:05.350 --> 18:07.250
Ellis...

18:07.250 --> 18:09.850
I'm going south.

18:09.850 --> 18:13.190
Because Wiñay Marka isn't here.

18:13.190 --> 18:15.520
Wiñay Marka?

18:15.520 --> 18:19.190
- Ellis?
- Stop watching me.

18:19.190 --> 18:21.730
Watch out for Nadie.

18:21.730 --> 18:23.920
I don't know what you mean.

18:27.200 --> 18:29.530
Maybe I rushed things a bit.

18:31.740 --> 18:33.870
It's all right, Ellis.

18:33.870 --> 18:36.210
I'll wait.

18:36.210 --> 18:40.150
You're certain to come to me, after all.

18:40.150 --> 18:43.150
Certain to come...

18:43.150 --> 18:44.910
Nadie!

18:56.600 --> 18:59.260
It looks like their reinforcements have arrived.

19:01.840 --> 19:04.670
Nadie.

19:04.670 --> 19:07.770
You dummy. I told you to hide, didn't I?

19:09.310 --> 19:12.280
But I'm glad you're okay.

19:16.780 --> 19:19.920
I'm sorry.

19:19.920 --> 19:21.580
Ellis.

19:33.430 --> 19:35.600
- This wasn't the place.
- What?

19:35.600 --> 19:37.470
Let's go south.

19:37.470 --> 19:39.140
Ellis...

19:39.140 --> 19:42.040
Wiñay Marka.

19:42.040 --> 19:44.030
Yeah, let's go.

19:56.960 --> 19:59.480
They sure are hard-working.

20:04.200 --> 20:05.860
That's it!

20:29.520 --> 20:31.530
All right, we're going to make a run for it!

20:31.530 --> 20:33.150
Yessir.

20:34.330 --> 20:36.400
1st Platoon!

20:36.400 --> 20:38.490
What? Withdraw?

20:46.340 --> 20:48.510
Roger that.

20:48.510 --> 20:51.510
Rosenberg, is it?

20:51.510 --> 20:55.180
I am deeply grateful for your assistance.

20:55.180 --> 20:56.880
For the good of the nation...

20:56.880 --> 21:00.520
I trust you spoke truthfully when you
told me that, my dear Rosenberg?

21:00.520 --> 21:05.750
Yes. When all is done,
you will be a hero, Senator.

21:07.930 --> 21:10.630
I will have faith in the German spirit.

21:10.630 --> 21:13.370
Thank you very much.

21:13.370 --> 21:15.770
To our future.

21:37.390 --> 21:41.090
- Not yet.
- Not yet, huh?

21:41.090 --> 21:44.120
- Same with that one.
- Same with this one, huh?

21:56.340 --> 22:00.410
She found out something there?

22:00.410 --> 22:03.250
But what?

22:03.250 --> 22:05.950
Could it be about herself?

22:10.290 --> 22:12.350
I'm going to protect her.

22:14.090 --> 22:16.600
Even if it costs me my life.

22:16.600 --> 22:18.300
- Not yet.
- Not yet, huh?

22:18.300 --> 22:21.460
- Same with that one.
- Same with this one, huh?

22:23.300 --> 22:25.270
On this day, the two of them...

22:25.270 --> 22:29.800
...each came to have a new
secret to be kept from the other.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
